    "image_caption": null,
    "content_html": "<div class=\"articlebodycontent col-xl-9 col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-12\" id=\"content-body-71682990\"><div class=\"schemaDiv\" id=\"schemaDiv\"><p><span class=\"drop-caps\">R</span>ecently, our village temple asked my daughter to offer a fistful of coins in each hand. The day before, I went hunting for these coins.</p><p>I searched every cupboard at home. The only coins I found were an American cent and a Dubai dirham. I wasn’t sure our deity accepted foreign currency. At tea stalls, paan shops and grocery stores, shopkeepers stared at me. “Sir, this is the UPI age!” I held out a ₹500 note and pleaded, “<i>Do-teen</i> coin <i>de de baba</i>! <i>Do-teen coin de de</i>!” A few kind souls saved the day.</p></div><div class=\"articleblock-container\" id=\"arthardpv\"></div><div class=\"update-publish-time article-published-time-end\"><p class=\"publish-time-new\"> Published <span>- November 15, 2026 04:23 am IST</span></p></div><div class=\"comments-shares share-page flex print-hide\" data-artid=\"71682990\" data-title=\"Two fistfuls of coins\" data-url=\"https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/open-page/two-fistfuls-of-coins/article71682990.ece\"><div class=\"left\"><div class=\"share\"><button class=\"btn share-btn\" data-ga-labelclick=\"ArticleShare\"></button><ul class=\"share-list bottom\" style=\"display: none;\"><li class=\"copy-link\" data-cf-modified-83a4b753bdea7a52b1432c4e-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; copytext('https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/open-page/two-fistfuls-of-coins/article71682990.ece');\">\n                Copy link  \n                        \n            </li><li class=\"email\"><a href=\"mailto:?subject=Two%20fistfuls%20of%20coins&amp;amp;body=Check%20out%20this%20link%20https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thehindu.com%2Fopinion%2Fopen-page%2Ftwo-fistfuls-of-coins%2Farticle71682990.ece\" target=\"_self\">\n                    Email     \n                                \n                </a></li><li class=\